The quotation is specifically about the planning system — land use regulation and development approval processes — where "blockers" (those who obstruct development) have been favoured over "builders" (those who want to construct). The core mechanism is land use planning regulation and its effect on housing/construction supply.

This maps to **R** — Urban, Rural, Regional, Real Estate, and Transportation Economics, specifically R5 (Regional Government Analysis) and R3 (Real Estate Markets, Spatial Production Analysis). The planning system as a regulatory barrier to construction also has a **K2** (Regulation and Business Law) dimension, but the substance is squarely about land use and development.

